llvm-3.7.1 local rule: the link stage's GVN does no scalar PRE

This patch CHANGES THE LINK STAGE ONLY (PassManagerBuilder::
addLTOOptimizationPasses): its GVN runs without scalar PRE (GVN.cpp
performPRE); load PRE and the rest of GVN are unchanged, and every per-unit
pipeline is unchanged. 3.7.1 has no option for this (EnablePRE, GVN.cpp:67,
gates load PRE as well, 1774 and 2361).

Census (round 296C, a report of every scalar PRE per stage, c296/res/
opt_ctl.err and u/ctl/err.txt): over the whole two-stage game module the
units' own GVN performs 136 scalar PREs in 133 functions (their rows are
equal: the base agrees); the link's GVN performs 3: 0x307330 and 0x402110
(the address of the state's +0x40, which stage 1 left as a phi of two equal
addresses: the base's `add rax, 0x40` in the join; the link hoists it and
the store takes `[rax+0x40]`) and draft 0xc1ac70 (a bitcast, no change in
its code). The base agrees with none of the link's three. Base context
(joinadd.py): 15 functions keep a join-block address and a store through
it, as the two rows do (0x4021a0 and 0x471a40 are unwritten siblings).

Swept alone (probe option -tlg-scalar-pre=false on the link's opt): 2
functions change, 0x307330 and 0x402110 become equal, no row lost, no
draft or witness changed (c290's -enable-pre=false at the link moved draft
0xc1ac70 from 81/97 to 43/97: load PRE; this rule leaves it at 81/97).

diff -ru a/include/llvm/Transforms/Scalar.h b/include/llvm/Transforms/Scalar.h
--- a/include/llvm/Transforms/Scalar.h
+++ b/include/llvm/Transforms/Scalar.h
@@ -338,7 +338,7 @@
 // GVN - This pass performs global value numbering and redundant load
 // elimination cotemporaneously.
 //
-FunctionPass *createGVNPass(bool NoLoads = false);
+FunctionPass *createGVNPass(bool NoLoads = false, bool NoScalarPRE = false);
 
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 //
diff -ru a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp
--- a/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/Scalar/GVN.cpp
@@ -590,6 +590,7 @@
 
   class GVN : public FunctionPass {
     bool NoLoads;
+    bool NoScalarPRE;
     MemoryDependenceAnalysis *MD;
     DominatorTree *DT;
     const TargetLibraryInfo *TLI;
@@ -616,8 +617,9 @@
 
   public:
     static char ID; // Pass identification, replacement for typeid
-    explicit GVN(bool noloads = false)
-        : FunctionPass(ID), NoLoads(noloads), MD(nullptr) {
+    explicit GVN(bool noloads = false, bool noscalarpre = false)
+        : FunctionPass(ID), NoLoads(noloads), NoScalarPRE(noscalarpre),
+          MD(nullptr) {
       initializeGVNPass(*PassRegistry::getPassRegistry());
     }
 
@@ -729,8 +731,8 @@
 }
 
 // The public interface to this file...
-FunctionPass *llvm::createGVNPass(bool NoLoads) {
-  return new GVN(NoLoads);
+FunctionPass *llvm::createGVNPass(bool NoLoads, bool NoScalarPRE) {
+  return new GVN(NoLoads, NoScalarPRE);
 }
 
 INITIALIZE_PASS_BEGIN(GVN, "gvn", "Global Value Numbering", false, false)
@@ -2358,7 +2360,7 @@
     ++Iteration;
   }
 
-  if (EnablePRE) {
+  if (EnablePRE && !NoScalarPRE) {
     // Fabricate val-num for dead-code in order to suppress assertion in
     // performPRE().
     assignValNumForDeadCode();
diff -ru a/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp b/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp
--- a/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp
+++ b/lib/Transforms/IPO/PassManagerBuilder.cpp
@@ -489,7 +489,9 @@
   PM.add(createLICMPass());                 // Hoist loop invariants.
   if (EnableMLSM)
     PM.add(createMergedLoadStoreMotionPass()); // Merge ld/st in diamonds.
-  PM.add(createGVNPass(DisableGVNLoadPRE)); // Remove redundancies.
+  // The link's GVN keeps what each unit's PRE left (no scalar PRE); loads
+  // are still made available across blocks.
+  PM.add(createGVNPass(DisableGVNLoadPRE, /*NoScalarPRE=*/true));
   PM.add(createMemCpyOptPass());            // Remove dead memcpys.
 
   // Nuke dead stores.
